.TH HEKON 1 "October 2026" "hekon 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hekon \- delete SOURCE files duplicated in a master TARGET directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hekon
[\fIoptions\fR]
\fISOURCE TARGET\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hekon
("she who works her will") finds files in
.I SOURCE
that duplicate files in
.I TARGET
(the master, never modified) and deletes them.
Without options it only lists what
.I would
be deleted and deletes nothing.
.PP
If identical files exist only within
.I SOURCE
(no copy in
.IR TARGET ),
one copy (the shortest-named) is kept and the rest are treated as duplicates.
Duplicate sets existing only within
.I TARGET
are ignored.
.PP
Content matching reuses the
.BR fdupes (1)
pipeline: file size, then partial and full XXH3 digests, then a
byte-for-byte confirmation before any file is listed or deleted.
.PP
Both directories are always recursed into. Symbolic links are not
followed; only regular files are considered. Hardlinks (same inode)
are never treated as duplicates.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-delete
Actually delete the SOURCE duplicates. Without this option,
.B hekon
is a dry run.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Hide the progress indicator.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " N"
Hash with N worker threads (1..64, default: online CPUs, max 8).
.TP
.B \-\-cache
Reuse file hashes across runs. Digests are keyed by device, inode,
size, mtime and ctime in a flat file under
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/hekon/
(or
.IR ~/.cache/hekon/ );
any change to those invalidates the entry. The byte-for-byte
confirmation still runs every time.
.TP
.B \-\-cache-clear
Delete the hash cache file and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-stats
Print a machine-parseable
.B stats:
line to stderr with exact counters (files, partial/full hashes,
full_reused_small, bytes_partial/full/saved, confirms) and wall-clock
timings (scan_ms, match_ms, total_ms), plus the active chunk_size and
partial_size. Used by
.B bench_hekon.sh
to verify optimizations.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Preview what would be removed from a download folder:
.RS
hekon ~/downloads ~/photos
.RE
.PP
Actually clean it:
.RS
hekon \-d ~/downloads ~/photos
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
Error (bad arguments, unreadable directory, overlapping SOURCE/TARGET).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fdupes (1)
